You are updating an existing rule-based extractor. Do NOT rewrite good rules; add or adjust only what is needed.

Task: German Legal Named Entity Recognition
Description: Recognize named entities in German legal text. Entities to look for: person. German capitalizes all nouns, so rules must use strong context anchors 

Input schema: {'text': 'str'}
Output schema:
entities: List[Entity]

Entity:
  text: string  # The matched text span
  start: integer  # Start character offset
  end: integer  # End character offset
  type: string  # Entity label

AVAILABLE ENTITY TYPES: ['person']
Rules MUST use one of these types in output_template.


DATA EVIDENCE FROM TRAINING:
- person (15 unique): "Dr.in Lorena H\u00f6welhans", "HR Sibylle Kadri", "Mag. Johann Fischerlehner", "RgR Juliette Wunsch, Bakk. techn.", "Cynthia Bernsdorff", "KommR Esra Flubacher", "Hon.-Prof.in Alina Lippart", "Dipl.-Ing. Dagobert Lautenschlager", "Univ.-Prof. Daniel Brauns", "Diethard Warmth, BA", "Mag. Ulrike Nussbaumer LL.M. M.B.L.", "Jonathan Kruijk", "Amber Leinveber", "Leif Meinking", "Priv.-Doz. Enrico M\u00f6hlenhof"
  Exact pattern: (?:Mag\. Ulrike Nussbaumer LL\.M\. M\.B\.L\.|(?:Dipl\.\-Ing\. Dagobert Lautenschlag|KommR Esra Flubach|Amber Leinveb)er|RgR Juliette Wunsch, Bakk\. techn\.|Priv\.\-Doz\. Enrico Möhlenhof|H(?:on\.\-Prof\.in Alina Lippart|R Sibylle Kadri)|Mag\. Johann Fischerlehner|Univ\.\-Prof\. Daniel Brauns|Dr\.in Lorena Höwelhans|Diethard Warmth, BA|Cynthia Bernsdorff|Jonathan Kruijk|Leif Meinking)
  In context: "...die Richterin [Dr.in Lorena H\u00f6welhans]  in der...", "...verstorbenen [HR Sibylle Kadri],  zuletzt wohnhaft...", "...durch den Richter [Mag. Johann Fischerlehner] in der ...", "... Beschwerdesache [RgR Juliette Wunsch, Bakk. techn.], Laabachstra\u00dfe 4,...", "...Mattighofen, und [Cynthia Bernsdorff], Laderding 53,..."

Note: Some entities contain multiple words; do NOT assume single-token matches.

Computed patterns match training strings only; generalize carefully.



